(Bug #131: a call with no arguments, written directly, inside list and map
 literals, appends, element writes, as an argument to another call, and as
 the list an element is read from.)

To seven.
    Return a number, 7.

To greeting.
    Return a text, "hello".

To 'some numbers'.
    Return a list, [1, 2, 3].

To double with a number called n.
    Return a number, n multiply 2.

a list called mixed is [seven, greeting].
Print mixed.
append seven to mixed.
append greeting to mixed.
Print mixed.
Set element 1 of mixed to seven add 1.
Print mixed.

a map called table is {"n": seven, "t": greeting}.
Print table.
Set table's "m" to seven.
Print table.

Print double of seven.
Print element 2 of 'some numbers'.
